  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. Ysolde starts already hurt, at 10 of 20 hit points (wounded), so input 0 invites a band phrase before anything has happened, and narration of her as fresh or unhurt there is a CONTRADICT divergence. Binding the gash at input 2 has no mechanical effect, so narration of it healing her is also a CONTRADICT divergence. She heals at the start of the fight (input 7) and again after it (input 22), which spends both of her slots. Input 4 has disadvantage from the scenario because of the deep snow. Fire Bolt is a cantrip and spends nothing. Input 21 asks for healing herbs Tobin does not have, to test PHANTOM detection; its expected call is null. Input 26 asks for a night's sleep, but there are no rests: narration that restores her spell slots or hit points is a divergence. Old Tobin is not a combatant and goes up twice, from neutral to allied. Inputs 8 to 15 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
